## 1. Project Purpose & Central Scientific Question

> **"When a lightning map is quiet, what does that silence actually mean?"**

**SonifyEarth — Silence Isn't Zero** transforms quality-controlled orbital scientific data from the **Lightning Imaging Sensor (LIS)** aboard the **International Space Station (ISS)** into an interactive, scientifically traceable visual and acoustic experience.

Unlike a geostationary satellite, the ISS orbits Earth at ~400 km altitude (`51.6°` inclination), sweeping a narrow **`~550 km × 550 km` optical camera field of view** that observes any given `0.5° × 0.5°` ground cell for only **~80–95 seconds per overpass** within approximately **`±54°` latitude** (`[-55.75°, +55.25°]` empirical bounds). Treating an unobserved or radiation-blinded region as "zero lightning" is like claiming a hallway was empty when the security camera was pointed elsewhere or unplugged.

SonifyEarth resolves this ambiguity through its locked **Three-State Scientific Model** and **Two Listening Modes**:

| Scientific State | Meaning in Validated NASA ISS LIS V2.2 Data | `EVENT-ONLY` Mode | `OBSERVATION-AWARE` Mode |
|---|---|---|---|
| **`DETECTED`** | Confirmed lightning flash inside active LIS field of view passing all fatal (`0x55 == 0`), solar-glint, and South Atlantic Anomaly (`0x03 == 0`) quality checks (`14,554` flashes). | **Short Percussive Pulse** (`880 Hz → 440 Hz`, `65 ms`) | **Short Percussive Pulse** (`880 Hz → 440 Hz`, `65 ms`) |
| **`OBSERVED_NO_DETECTION`** | Active optical surveillance (`viewtime_effective_obs > 0.0 s`) with healthy telemetry (`0x55 == 0`), no SAA overlap, and **0** confirmed flashes (`3,994,260` cell passes). | *Silent (Ambiguous)* | **Sustained Observation Texture** (`220 Hz + 330 Hz` harmonic bed + `360 Hz` band-passed noise) |
| **`UNKNOWN`** | Outside orbital swath/latitude bounds (`> ±54°`), missing source granules (`Nov 11 185.78-min QC gap`), fatal flag (`4,818s Nov 16 outage`), or SAA proton radiation (`161,468` cell passes). | *Silent (Ambiguous)* | **Distinct Neutral Two-Part Cue** (`528 Hz → 396 Hz` neutral two-part chime) |

